## Setup

{%- if language == 'ts' %}

Needs Node 24 (`.nvmrc`), pnpm (`corepack enable`) and lefthook.

```bash
pnpm install
lefthook install
```
{%- elif language == 'python' %}

Needs [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) (it installs Python {{ '3.14' }} itself) and lefthook.

```bash
uv sync
lefthook install
```
{%- else %}

```bash
lefthook install
```
{%- endif %}
{%- if shape in ['ts-cli', 'python-cli', 'python-service', 'react-web'] %}

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill it in. Settings come only from the
environment; `.env` is never committed.
{%- endif %}

## Usage
{% if shape == 'ts-library' %}
```ts
import { greet } from '{{ project_name }}';
```

Document every export here: what it takes, what it returns, and its edge cases.

Apps use this library as a vendored copy:

```bash
pnpm run vendor -- ../my-app/vendor/{{ project_name }}
```
{%- elif shape == 'ts-cli' %}
```bash
pnpm start run --dry-run   # show what a run would do; changes nothing
pnpm start run             # do it (applies pending migrations first)
pnpm start status          # recent runs
```
{%- elif shape == 'python-cli' %}
```bash
uv run --env-file .env {{ project_name }} run --dry-run   # show what a run would do
uv run --env-file .env {{ project_name }} run             # do it
uv run --env-file .env {{ project_name }} status          # recent runs
```
{%- elif shape == 'python-service' %}
```bash
docker compose up -d db
uv run --env-file .env alembic upgrade head
uv run --env-file .env uvicorn {{ package_name }}.main:app --reload
```
{%- elif shape == 'react-web' %}
```bash
