### Schedule
{% if schedule == 'actions' %}
`.github/workflows/scheduled.yml` runs the job daily on GitHub Actions (edit
the cron line to change the time). Each run restores the SQLite database from
the `state` branch and saves it back afterwards (`ops/state.sh`), so the state
is as public as the repo. Run it by hand from the Actions tab (Run workflow);
manual runs are dry runs unless you untick the box. Put settings in the repo's
Actions secrets and variables and map them in the workflow's `env`. GitHub
emails you when a run fails, and so does ntfy if the `NTFY_URL` secret is set.
GitHub pauses schedules in public repos after 60 days without activity; the
state commits count as activity.
{%- else %}
`ops/launchd/install.sh` installs a launchd agent that runs the job daily
(edit the plist to change the time). Logs go to `~/Library/Logs/{{ project_name }}/`.
If `NTFY_URL` is set, a failed run sends a push notification.
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}

## Development

{%- if language == 'ts' %}

```bash
pnpm run test        # tests
pnpm run typecheck   # tsc --noEmit
pnpm run lint        # biome check
pnpm run format      # biome check --write
```
{%- elif language == 'python' %}

```bash
uv run pytest               # tests (network tests: uv run pytest -m live)
uv run mypy                 # type check
uv run ruff check           # lint
uv run ruff format          # format
```
{%- endif %}

Hooks run format and lint on commit, and typecheck and tests on push. Commit
messages follow `type(scope): Imperative subject` (see `CLAUDE.md`).
